  "description": "HAR-130 claim-code test vectors, shared by the API (TypeScript) and the device (Go). Normalizing: remove '-' and ASCII whitespace (space, tab, LF, CR, VT, FF); upper-case ASCII a-z only; map O to 0 and I and L to 1; then the result must be exactly 12 symbols of 0123456789ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTVWXYZ. Any other character (any non-ASCII one included) is invalid. normalized is null when the input must be refused with 400. hash is lowercase hex SHA-256 of UTF-8 'meatgeek-claim-v1:<deviceId>:<normalized>'; a claimant hash is the same over 'meatgeek-claimant-v1:<userId>'.",
